{"id": "EUVD-2026-55595", "enisaUuid": "252ad135-8330-3c96-8074-e8fce937b84a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: defer link RX stats percpu free to RCU\n\nsta_remove_link() frees a removed MLO link's RX stats percpu buffer right\naway, but defers only the link container to RCU:\n\n\tsta_info_free_link(&alloc->info);\n\tkfree_rcu(alloc, rcu_head);\n\nThe RX fast path reads link_sta under rcu_read_lock and writes the percpu\nstats. A reader that resolved link_sta before the removal keeps the\npointer. The container stays alive from the kfree_rcu, so the read still\nworks. But the percpu block it points to is already freed. This needs\nuses_rss. That is when pcpu_rx_stats exists.\n\nThe full STA teardown frees the deflink stats only after\nsynchronize_net(). The link removal path had no such barrier. The race is\nhard to win in practice, but the free should still wait for RCU.\n\nFree the link together with its data from a single RCU callback, so the\npercpu block is reclaimed only after readers drain.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:03", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5afc00280986063f1c355821544fabbb2a960f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b679c1cffb2f3d0854b8b05ea9e909ad6489046f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aa1789880fa5e41049b0f6a74a4fc2fa1997610", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a03fceae0c65b31ce31840dac5e26684ceecb65b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa2eb62525188269cdd402a583b9a8ed94657ff0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68409", "GHSA-g5f7-qj4q-4w5v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0879b939-e31a-3a7b-ab42-a3cdb1dca1a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "248d07ac-34a9-3b00-9868-fa251ffd0f5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "35f5b7bd-d731-3761-b5bc-d7996ca2a958", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c71420db653aba30a234d1e4cf86dde376e604fa <aa2eb62525188269cdd402a583b9a8ed94657ff0"}, {"id": "41e67780-0e40-3d3c-8c1e-0dab0415a198", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "43808838-33d2-3271-a123-12bad57d8f74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "488effc0-5b01-392c-a815-9e0fcca0757f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c71420db653aba30a234d1e4cf86dde376e604fa <b679c1cffb2f3d0854b8b05ea9e909ad6489046f"}, {"id": "6a1d8e4f-f596-3b91-a31a-a5367955c566", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c71420db653aba30a234d1e4cf86dde376e604fa <a03fceae0c65b31ce31840dac5e26684ceecb65b"}, {"id": "7003f337-cf9a-3cb0-b639-977b92882b82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "98f26ed6-61be-35e4-ad9d-daf115eb05ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "b8f2baed-d85e-3c87-b5cc-a97d64dcec90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c71420db653aba30a234d1e4cf86dde376e604fa <2aa1789880fa5e41049b0f6a74a4fc2fa1997610"}, {"id": "cf2c06cd-73be-3f64-8247-e89bbeca97b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "f1de7f74-44cb-3ef7-ac86-15dfbca0962d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c71420db653aba30a234d1e4cf86dde376e604fa <a5afc00280986063f1c355821544fabbb2a960f7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c3f13447-541e-383a-a299-b763d81c0e1a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}